### Geometry: the default setup (DetectorConstruction.cc, z = 0 at the ground) plus the target in
### which muons stop and form muonic atoms, whose X-rays the Compton detector (the Si/YSO stack)
### sees: a 20 x 20 x 1 cm aluminium panel centred above the stack (20 x 20 cm, top face at
### z = 31.6 cm), at z = 35.5 to 36.5 cm: 3.9 cm above the stack and 1 cm below the Al2 plate under
### the middle TOF (bottom face at z = 37.5 cm). Not supported by anything in the model.
### The free space between the stack top and Al2 is 5.9 cm. Another target: centre z = 31.6 cm +
### gap + thickness / 2, with gap + thickness <= 5.9 cm.
### Check it with macro/vis_target.mac; muons that stop in it end in the volume "Target" (end_vol).

/tof/target/enable true
/tof/target/material G4_Al
/tof/target/size 20 20 1 cm
/tof/target/position 0 0 36.0 cm
/update
